// Propulsion. PLACEHOLDER NUMBERS, all for feel only: thrust, torque and rated speeds were set on 12 Oct 2026 for
// the agility target "Agile" (GDR-0042: Halvex Runner 90° in ~0.8 s, 0 → ~22 m/s in ~2.5 s; small ships
// snappier), about 16× the concept-board thrust; gimbal values are invented.
// Engines push towards the part's forward side and may sit anywhere (GDR-0039); `gimbal` swings their thrust a
// few degrees to either side. `rated_speed` (GDR-0041): the thrust fades out as the ship's speed along the push
// direction approaches it, so the fastest engines pushing a way set the top speed that way. `plume` (GDR-0039,
// GDR-0049): the exhaust reaches `length` m behind the engine and burns the first part in its path (the ship's
// own, enemies and wrecks; never other vessels of the same owner) with `damage` and `heat` per second at full
// thrust, scaled by the thrust it gives. PLACEHOLDER plume numbers (lead, 12 Oct 2026): a torch drive held on a
// raider for about a second wrecks a part or two; an engine buried in the hull burns through an armour block in
// a second or two. Gyros turn the ship without thrust; RCS pods fire a nozzle out of every side that is open to
// space (they have no plume).
// Power tier: everything that moves the ship is `Normal` (the default), so thrust and turning brown out together.
[
    (
        id: "thruster",
        name: "Thruster",
        summary: "A small engine. Its exhaust burns whatever is right behind it.",
